{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1828 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "fb4908871f3ddd3bbb719a8a867bf79848026be968a2a62c47f488f32831ae38" :edb/db-before-t 1827 :edb/db-after-t 1828 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535140 50 #inst "2026-10-08T17:51:22.315Z" 13194139535140 true] [17592186133689 1020 #edb/ref 17592186333378 13194139535140 true] [17592186133689 1020 #edb/ref 17592186333385 13194139535140 true] [17592186133788 1020 #edb/ref 17592186333364 13194139535140 true] [17592186133788 1020 #edb/ref 17592186333371 13194139535140 true] [17592186134469 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535140 true] [17592186134469 1100 "Given that $⟨ \\cdot, \\cdot ⟩$ is the standard Hermitian inner product over $C$, find $⟨5a - 2b, c⟩$ if\n\n$⟨c, a⟩ =-1 + \\textrm{i}$ and $⟨b, c⟩ = 3 - 2\\textrm{i}$." 13194139535140 false] [17592186134469 1100 "Given that $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ is the standard Hermitian inner product over $C,$ find $⟨5a-2b,\\,c⟩$ if \n\n$\\,$ $⟨c,a⟩=-1+\\text{i}\\,$ and $\\,⟨b,c⟩=3-2\\text{i}.$" 13194139535140 true] [17592186134469 1145 "Recall that the inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties. \n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nFirst, we use the fact that the inner product over $C$ is linear in the first argument: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨5a-2b,\\,c⟩ & =⟨5a,c⟩-⟨2b,c⟩ \\\\  & =5⟨a,c⟩-2⟨b,c⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we use the fact that the inner product over $C$ has conjugate symmetry: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5⟨a,c⟩-2⟨b,c⟩ & =5\\overset{―}{⟨c,a⟩}-2⟨b,c⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute the values for $⟨c,a⟩$ and $⟨b,c⟩:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5\\overset{―}{⟨c,a⟩}-2⟨b,c⟩ & =5(\\overset{―}{-1+\\text{i}})-2(3-2\\text{i}) \\\\  & =5(-1-\\text{i})-2(3-2\\text{i}) \\\\  & =-5-5\\text{i}-6+4\\text{i} \\\\  & =-11-\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535140 true] [17592186333364 1017 #edb/ref 17592186333365 13194139535140 true] [17592186333364 1089 "q-141162" 13194139535140 true] [17592186333364 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535140 true] [17592186333364 1100 "Given that $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ is the standard Hermitian inner product over $C,$ find $⟨a,\\,2b+(3-2\\text{i})c⟩$ if \n\n$\\,$ $⟨b,a⟩=1-\\text{i}\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,c⟩=3\\text{i}.$" 13194139535140 true] [17592186333364 1113 #uuid "0f409f0a-d1f3-5a6f-b4c4-c490f83517f4" 13194139535140 true] [17592186333364 1145 "Recall that the inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties. \n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nFirst, we use the fact that the inner product over $C$ is antilinear in the second argument:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨a,\\,2b+(3-2\\text{i})c⟩ & =⟨a,2b⟩+⟨a,(3-2\\text{i})c⟩ \\\\  & =\\overset{―}{2}⟨a,b⟩+(\\overset{―}{3-2\\text{i}})⟨a,c⟩ \\\\  & =2⟨a,b⟩+(3+2\\text{i})⟨a,c⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that the inner product over $C$ has conjugate symmetry:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2⟨a,b⟩+(3+2\\text{i})⟨a,c⟩ & =2\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}+(3+2\\text{i})⟨a,c⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute the values for $⟨b,a⟩$ and $⟨a,c⟩:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}+(3+2\\text{i})⟨a,c⟩ & =2\\cdot \\overset{―}{1-\\text{i}}+(3+2\\text{i})\\cdot (3\\text{i}) \\\\  & =2\\cdot (1+\\text{i})-6+9\\text{i} \\\\  & =-4+11\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535140 true] [17592186333365 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333366 13194139535140 true] [17592186333365 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333367 13194139535140 true] [17592186333365 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333368 13194139535140 true] [17592186333365 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333369 13194139535140 true] [17592186333365 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333370 13194139535140 true] [17592186333365 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535140 true] [17592186333365 1041 "selection" 13194139535140 true] [17592186333365 1104 #edb/ref 17592186333369 13194139535140 true] [17592186333365 1110 #uuid "bccea3f0-485f-5dae-94e4-fcbdad249dfc" 13194139535140 true] [17592186333366 1034 "-4+8\\text{i}" 13194139535140 true] [17592186333366 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535140 true] [17592186333366 1111 #uuid "aab14461-fafd-5ce8-a827-b7fbcd8ba123" 13194139535140 true] [17592186333367 1034 "8-4\\text{i}" 13194139535140 true] [17592186333367 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535140 true] [17592186333367 1111 #uuid "632d4c5b-412e-5d54-8287-deafd0eb4f50" 13194139535140 true] [17592186333368 1034 "11+8\\text{i}" 13194139535140 true] [17592186333368 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535140 true] [17592186333368 1111 #uuid "bbb1f13b-8ee6-5ffa-a10a-2c6c4e3eeb9e" 13194139535140 true] [17592186333369 1034 "-4+11\\text{i}" 13194139535140 true] [17592186333369 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535140 true] [17592186333369 1111 #uuid "5673cb0f-58ae-5230-9bed-341314357b1d" 13194139535140 true] [17592186333370 1034 "7+6\\text{i}" 13194139535140 true] [17592186333370 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535140 true] [17592186333370 1111 #uuid "e3a10379-ceca-5e6e-8aa5-185c292e236c" 13194139535140 true] [17592186333371 1017 #edb/ref 17592186333372 13194139535140 true] [17592186333371 1089 "q-97200" 13194139535140 true] [17592186333371 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535140 true] [17592186333371 1100 "Given that $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ is the standard Hermitian inner product over $C,$ find $⟨\\text{i}a,\\,b+c⟩$ if \n\n  $⟨a,b⟩=3-2\\text{i}\\,$ and $\\,⟨c,a⟩=2+\\text{i}.$" 13194139535140 true] [17592186333371 1113 #uuid "bd73aa00-9e5a-5eba-8caf-b97d3032b2dd" 13194139535140 true] [17592186333371 1145 "Recall that the inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties. \n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nFirst, we use the fact that the inner product over $C$ is linear in the first argument: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨\\text{i}a,\\,b+c⟩ & =⟨\\text{i}a,b⟩+⟨\\text{i}a,c⟩ \\\\  & =\\text{i}⟨a,b⟩+\\text{i}⟨a,c⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nNext, we use the fact that the inner product over $C$ has conjugate symmetry: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{i}⟨a,b⟩+\\text{i}⟨a,c⟩ & =\\text{i}⟨a,b⟩+\\text{i}\\overset{―}{⟨c,a⟩}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute the values for $⟨a,b⟩$ and $⟨c,a⟩:$    \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{i}⟨a,b⟩+\\text{i}\\overset{―}{⟨c,a⟩} & =\\text{i}(3-2\\text{i})+\\text{i}\\overset{―}{(2+\\text{i})} \\\\  & =\\text{i}(3-2\\text{i})+\\text{i}(2-\\text{i}) \\\\  & =2+3\\text{i}+1+2\\text{i} \\\\  & =3+5\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535140 true] [17592186333372 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333373 13194139535140 true] [17592186333372 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333374 13194139535140 true] [17592186333372 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333375 13194139535140 true] [17592186333372 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333376 13194139535140 true] [17592186333372 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333377 13194139535140 true] [17592186333372 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535140 true] [17592186333372 1041 "selection" 13194139535140 true] [17592186333372 1104 #edb/ref 17592186333376 13194139535140 true] [17592186333372 1110 #uuid "c0ec2b6a-0e60-5928-bcbc-9af9c861bb3d" 13194139535140 true] [17592186333373 1034 "2-3\\text{i}" 13194139535140 true] [17592186333373 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535140 true] [17592186333373 1111 #uuid "708e87bf-0009-52aa-a36d-60eb806f7f03" 13194139535140 true] [17592186333374 1034 "-2\\text{i}" 13194139535140 true] [17592186333374 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535140 true] [17592186333374 1111 #uuid "4bc6aff1-cee8-5a14-848d-6ce0a2bf9575" 13194139535140 true] [17592186333375 1034 "5\\text{i}" 13194139535140 true] [17592186333375 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535140 true] [17592186333375 1111 #uuid "18a3c178-1ff7-5dbe-8f43-909f93b3cd04" 13194139535140 true] [17592186333376 1034 "3+5\\text{i}" 13194139535140 true] [17592186333376 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535140 true] [17592186333376 1111 #uuid "05ac0162-68fd-579d-a436-b9959555b924" 13194139535140 true] [17592186333377 1034 "5-2\\text{i}" 13194139535140 true] [17592186333377 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535140 true] [17592186333377 1111 #uuid "6b3075fc-47fc-505e-a92d-6e8cd526f02c" 13194139535140 true] [17592186333378 1017 #edb/ref 17592186333379 13194139535140 true] [17592186333378 1089 "q-97229" 13194139535140 true] [17592186333378 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535140 true] [17592186333378 1100 "Consider the standard Hermitian inner product $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ over $C.$ \nWhich of the following statements are true? \n\n- $⟨a,b⟩=⟨b,a⟩$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$\n- $⟨ia,ia⟩=⟨a,a⟩$ for any $a\\in {C}^{n}$\n- $⟨a,b⟩\\in R$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$" 13194139535140 true] [17592186333378 1113 #uuid "5ab6fe43-e2b9-5b59-8ea1-dcdc03dc098d" 13194139535140 true] [17592186333378 1145 "Recall that the standard Hermitian inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties:\n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. The inner product over $C$ has conjugate symmetry.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, by the linearity in the first argument  and the antilinearity in the second argument we have\n\n$$\n⟨ia,ia⟩=(i\\cdot \\overset{¯}{i})⟨a,a⟩=-{i}^{2}⟨a,a⟩=⟨a,a⟩.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. The inner product over $C$ is a complex number, in general.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139535140 true] [17592186333379 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333380 13194139535140 true] [17592186333379 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333381 13194139535140 true] [17592186333379 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333382 13194139535140 true] [17592186333379 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333383 13194139535140 true] [17592186333379 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333384 13194139535140 true] [17592186333379 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535140 true] [17592186333379 1041 "selection" 13194139535140 true] [17592186333379 1104 #edb/ref 17592186333384 13194139535140 true] [17592186333379 1110 #uuid "f94aa2ec-a9b4-5877-bfdd-f40e275d7465" 13194139535140 true] [17592186333380 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535140 true] [17592186333380 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535140 true] [17592186333380 1111 #uuid "c84b31c4-3526-50e5-a51f-0d53d3c27337" 13194139535140 true] [17592186333381 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535140 true] [17592186333381 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535140 true] [17592186333381 1111 #uuid "df6d73d5-6d50-54cc-b1fa-9c9d6d1bec88" 13194139535140 true] [17592186333382 1034 "I only" 13194139535140 true] [17592186333382 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535140 true] [17592186333382 1111 #uuid "17c7ea01-8fc8-54f2-b2ce-c2dc0bf9fbb6" 13194139535140 true] [17592186333383 1034 "III only" 13194139535140 true] [17592186333383 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535140 true] [17592186333383 1111 #uuid "ef684b99-302a-5ad7-be72-e8a883994091" 13194139535140 true] [17592186333384 1034 "II only" 13194139535140 true] [17592186333384 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535140 true] [17592186333384 1111 #uuid "e605551c-cb0d-5188-9dcc-edc6fa29a156" 13194139535140 true] [17592186333385 1017 #edb/ref 17592186333386 13194139535140 true] [17592186333385 1089 "q-97306" 13194139535140 true] [17592186333385 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535140 true] [17592186333385 1100 "Consider the standard Hermitian inner product $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ over $C.$ \nWhich of the following statements are true? \n\n- $⟨a,-ia⟩=-i⟨a,a⟩$ for any nonzero vector  $a\\in {C}^{n}$\n- $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$\n- $⟨a,b⟩\\in R$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$" 13194139535140 true] [17592186333385 1113 #uuid "43072e08-2c50-58fc-b70f-e161da4c2358" 13194139535140 true] [17592186333385 1145 "Recall that the standard Hermitian inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties:\n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false.  By the antilinearity of $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$  in the second argument we have \n\n$$\n⟨a,-ia⟩=\\overset{―}{(-i)}⟨a,a⟩=i⟨a,a⟩\\ne -i⟨a,a⟩\n$$\n\n \nfor any nonzero vector  $a\\in {C}^{n}.$\n\n- Statement II  is true. Indeed, the inner product over $C$ has conjugate symmetry.\n\n- Statement III is false. The inner product over $C$ is a complex number in general.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139535140 true] [17592186333386 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333387 13194139535140 true] [17592186333386 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333388 13194139535140 true] [17592186333386 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333389 13194139535140 true] [17592186333386 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333390 13194139535140 true] [17592186333386 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333391 13194139535140 true] [17592186333386 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535140 true] [17592186333386 1041 "selection" 13194139535140 true] [17592186333386 1104 #edb/ref 17592186333391 13194139535140 true] [17592186333386 1110 #uuid "da09a662-bd62-5029-aed0-11a8572d60f4" 13194139535140 true] [17592186333387 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535140 true] [17592186333387 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535140 true] [17592186333387 1111 #uuid "41589c99-7f3e-58b6-aca3-8b6b3d5aebb5" 13194139535140 true] [17592186333388 1034 "I only" 13194139535140 true] [17592186333388 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535140 true] [17592186333388 1